  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC Phase-Out Management Plan (Stage II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project involves the second stage of Rwanda&apos;s HCFC Phase-Out Management Plan (HPMP), covering the period from January 2025 to De cember 2027. Its objectives include strengthening enforcement of ozone-depleting substance regulations, developing standards for energy-efficient low-GWP refrigerants, updating training curricula for customs and RAC technicians, and establishing centers of excellence for training and refrigerant recovery. The total funding requested is $200 ,000, with UNEP receiving $117,000 and UNIDO $83,000, excluding support costs. Activities will include capacity building, technology promotion for low-GWP alternatives, public awareness campaigns, and a national product registration system to promote green technologies and energy efficiency in the refrigeration and air conditioning sector.</narrative>
  </description>
